# Development journal

At the end of any session that changes code, config or docs, add an entry to the top of `docs/JOURNAL.md`, below the header and above the previous newest entry.

Each entry covers:
- Date and session, plus the bucket or area
- What changed
- Why
- Decisions made (put lasting ones in `docs/DECISIONS.md` too)
- Unvalidated parameters or assumptions
- Anything not verified (for example, tests not run)
- Next steps and open questions

Write in plain, complete sentences for the user, not agent shorthand. Separate entries with `---`.

`CHANGELOG.md` stays separate: a terse one-line entry for each trading-logic change or bug fix.

Keep `docs/VISION.md` section 12 (build status) current. It is the only copy of the vision document.
